A matrix that is simpler than <<ref:rwt>> can be constructed for most concrete quivers. For example, Section <<ref:mtp>> shows that the matrix

\begin{equation*}
M(x):=\begin{bmatrix}
1&0&0&0&0&x_{\alpha }&x_{\beta }\\
0&2&0&1&0&x_{\gamma}&0\\
0&0&3&0&1&x_{\delta }&x_{\zeta}\\
0&0&0&4&0&1&0\\
0&0&0&0&5&x_{\varepsilon}&1\\
0&0&0&0&0&6&0\\
0&0&0&0&0&0&7
\end{bmatrix}
\end{equation*}

can be used in Lemma <<ref:njp>> instead of <<ref:nkl>>.
